From: Xbox360 Blades <xbox360-blades@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 16:26:53 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 16/52] Dashboard memory area (2858): list, details and delete
 content and profiles

Read from 2858 xam and the dashboard:
- XamContentAggregateCreateEnumerator for system titles walks
  Content\<xuid>\<title>\<type>\<package> as xam does (xuid 0 = all users,
  title 0 = all, type -1 = all) and returns xam's 0x148-byte records
  (content data, owner at 0x138, title at 0x140).
- XamContentGetAttributesInternal: {attributes, 3 times, size} (0x24).
- XamContentGetMetaDataInternal: the package header's metadata block
  (0x93D6 bytes from offset 0x344): type, size, title, creator, display
  name, thumbnail, and the game's name/icon from a profile's GPD for it.
- XamProfileLoadAccountInfo, XamGetDefaultSystemImage (xam's own
  defaultsystemimage.png), XamUniSortCmpString (runs xam's own code).
- Delete: "Delete Profile Only" = XamContentDeleteInternal of the profile
  package (saves stay, profile signed out); "Delete Profile and Items" =
  XamProfileDelete (profile and all it owns).
- The hard drive is called "Hard Drive", as the console does.
- XamShowMessageBoxUI logs the chosen button.

